1. Checking
Check that the station’s coordinates does not change.


Code
station_coordinate_check &lt;- pm25_daily |&gt;
  distinct(NAPS_ID, Latitude, Longitude) |&gt;
  count(NAPS_ID, name = "coordinate_versions") |&gt;
  filter(coordinate_versions &gt; 1)

station_coordinate_check


# A tibble: 0 × 2
# ℹ 2 variables: NAPS_ID &lt;dbl&gt;, coordinate_versions &lt;int&gt;


The result confirms that the each station’s coordinates did not change.
For this, going to use geosphere.
*Important: geosphere expects coordinates in c(Longitude, Latitude) order

Using OUT_DATE
Calculating the duration of the fire in days by finding the difference between reported dates of fire and the date the fire was put out.


Code
# calculate duration through OUT_DATE
large_fires_bc |&gt;
  filter(!is.na(OUT_DATE)) |&gt;
  mutate(duration_days = as.numeric(difftime(OUT_DATE, REP_DATE, units = "days"))) |&gt;
  summarise(
    min_duration = min(duration_days),
    median_duration = median(duration_days),
    mean_duration = mean(duration_days),
    max_duration = max(duration_days)
  )


# A tibble: 1 × 4
  min_duration median_duration mean_duration max_duration
         &lt;dbl&gt;           &lt;dbl&gt;         &lt;dbl&gt;        &lt;dbl&gt;
1           -2            93.5          97.6          325


The min_duration of -2 shows that there are inconsistencies.


Code
# find out which row gives a duration days below 0
large_fires_bc |&gt;
  filter(!is.na(OUT_DATE)) |&gt;
  mutate(duration_days = as.numeric(difftime(OUT_DATE, REP_DATE, units = "days"))) |&gt;
  filter(duration_days &lt; 0) |&gt;
  select(
    NFDBFIREID,
    FIRENAME,
    REP_DATE,
    OUT_DATE,
    duration_days,
    SIZE_HA,
    MORE_INFO
  )


